<details><summary>Scope of the mathematics</summary>
These reductions do not resolve global existence and smoothness. A full partial-regularity application still needs a concrete scale-invariant velocity-pressure excess, a local epsilon-regularity theorem for suitable weak solutions, and a parabolic covering estimate. Spectral cascade direction likewise needs more than total conservation.
</details>
